steps.body:
A `std::priority_queue<T>`, also from `<queue>`, always gives you the largest element first. It is a *max-heap*: a binary tree packed into a `std::vector`, so `push` and `pop` are O(log n) and `top` is O(1).

```cpp
std::priority_queue<int> pq;
pq.push(3);
pq.push(9);
pq.push(1);
std::cout << pq.top() << '\n';  // 9
```

It does not keep everything sorted. Only the top is guaranteed, and you cannot loop over it or index it. Drain it with the usual pattern: copy `top()`, then `pop()`.

For smallest first, pass the underlying container and `std::greater` from `<functional>`:

```cpp
std::priority_queue<int, std::vector<int>, std::greater<int>> minHeap;
for (int x : {3, 9, 1}) minHeap.push(x);
std::cout << minHeap.top() << '\n';  // 1, the smallest
```

Pairs compare by `first`, then by `second`, so a heap of `(minutes, name)` pairs orders by minutes and breaks ties by name. Unpack the top with structured bindings:

```cpp harness
#include <bits/stdc++.h>

int main() {
    using Task = std::pair<int, std::string>;
    std::priority_queue<Task, std::vector<Task>, std::greater<Task>> pq;
    pq.push({25, "report"});
    pq.push({5, "email"});
    pq.push({15, "review"});
    {{code}}
    std::cout << name << " takes " << minutes << " min\n";
    std::cout << pq.size() << " left\n";
    return 0;
}
```

```cpp
auto [minutes, name] = pq.top();  // a copy, safe to keep
pq.pop();
```

> Gotcha: `const auto& [minutes, name] = pq.top();` binds to the element inside the heap, and `pop()` moves other elements into that slot, so the names then read the wrong pair. With one element left, they dangle. Use plain `auto`. As always, `top()` on an empty heap is undefined behavior.

example.code:
#include <functional>
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <string>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>

using Task = std::pair<int, std::string>;

int main() {
    const std::vector<int> priorities = {3, 9, 1, 7};
    std::priority_queue<int> maxHeap;
    for (int p : priorities) {
        maxHeap.push(p);
    }
    std::string line = "";
    while (!maxHeap.empty()) {
        int p = maxHeap.top();
        maxHeap.pop();
        if (!line.empty()) {
            line += ' ';
        }
        line += std::to_string(p);
    }
    std::cout << line << '\n';

    std::priority_queue<Task, std::vector<Task>, std::greater<Task>> tasks;
    tasks.push({25, "report"});
    tasks.push({5, "email"});
    tasks.push({15, "review"});
    tasks.push({5, "call"});
    while (!tasks.empty()) {
        auto [minutes, name] = tasks.top();
        tasks.pop();
        std::cout << name << " takes " << minutes << " min" << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}

